Feature: Running and stopping a program
  When you click LAUNCH, the launcher starts the program and opens the LOG screen. The LOG
  screen shows the output of the program, and its state beside its name. While the program
  runs, LAUNCH becomes STOP. Click STOP to end the program.

  Expectation: LAUNCH starts the program, and becomes STOP
    The LOG screen shows the output of the program, and its command line in the first line.
    The launcher runs one program at a time. To start another, stop the one that runs.

    Given the program is idle
    When the pilot launches
    Then the program is running
    And the launch button is STOP

  Expectation: STOP ends the program
    STOP ends the program and all that it started: the sim, ArduPilot and the console.

    Given the program is running
    When the pilot stops the program
    Then the program is stopped
    And the launch button is LAUNCH
